issolved solids in mg/L\n- ✓ `conductivity_us_cm` - Conductivity in microSiemens/cm\n\n**pH:**\n- ✓ `ph` - stored in WaterState and derived from alkalinity/DIC\n\n---\n\n### Display Formulas - ALL CORRECTLY IMPLEMENTED\n\nLine 79-80 in snapshot.rs shows exact formula match:\n```rust\nlet gh_d = ((2.497 * ca_mg_l) + (4.118 * mg_mg_l)) / 17.848;\nlet kh_d = (alkalinity_meq_l * 50.0) / 17.848;\n```\n\nLine 77-78 shows TDS and conductivity:\n```rust\nlet tds_mg_l = safe_div(total_tracked_ions_mg, volume_l);\nlet conductivity_us_cm = tds_mg_l / 0.65;\n```\n\npH derivation (chemistry.rs lines 7-21):\n- Computed from alkalinity and DIC using Henderson-Hasselbalch equation\n- Formula: `6.3 + log10(alkalinity_meq_l) - log10(dic_mmol_l)` clamped to [5.5, 8.5]\n\nNH3 computation (chemistry.rs lines 23-27):\n- Uses Henderson-Hasselbalch with temperature-dependent pKa\n- Fraction of NH3 = 1 / (1 + 10^(pKa - pH))\n\n---\n\n### Unit Consistency\n\n**Storage Convention (WaterState):**\n- All dissolved pools stored as **total amounts in mg** (or meq for alkalinity)\n- This follows the naming convention with `_total` suffix\n\n**Source Water Convention (SourceWaterProfile):**\n- All source water chemistry stored as **per-liter concentrations** (mg/L or meq/L)\n- This is clear from field names ending in `_per_l`\n- Multiplication by `volume_l` converts to totals when initializing WaterState\n\n**Display Convention (TankSnapshot):**\n- All display values in **concentrations** (mg/L or degrees or uS/cm)\n- Conversion from totals done via safe division: `total / volume_l`\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\nAll required dissolved pools and derived display values are present and correctly implemented. The units follow a consistent convention: storage as totals, display as concentrations. All formulas match the specified requirements exactly.\n\n**No missing pools or formulas detected.**"}],"totalDurationMs":39474,"totalTokens":33527,"totalToolUseCount":15,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_in