{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XhHENGYXj4UW1xu3YwzppQ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me compile my comprehensive findings. All ten systems have been verified. Let me create a summary report:\n\n## VERIFICATION REPORT: Tank Simulation Systems Implementation\n\nAll 10 major simulation systems are **FULLY IMPLEMENTED** with correct formulas and constants. Here's the detailed verification:\n\n---\n\n### 1. TEMPERATURE MODEL - IMPLEMENTED\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/temperature.rs`\n\n- **UA-based heat transfer**: Fully implemented (lines 48-53)\n  - `ua_total_w_per_k = (k_surface * surface_area_m2 * top_factor) + (k_wall * wall_area_m2)`\n  - Heat capacity: 4186 J/L·K (line 39)\n  - Time step: 3600 seconds (hourly) (line 33)\n\n- **Heater logic with deadband**: Implemented (lines 55-63)\n  - Fires when enabled AND water < (setpoint - deadband/2)\n  - Never cools: Only adds heat, never subtracts\n\n- **Key constants**: k_surface and k_wall from process params (lines 45-46)\n\n---\n\n### 2. NITROGEN CYCLE - FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs`\n\n**Complete pathway**: detritus → mineralization → TAN → nitrite → nitrate\n\n- **Feed leaching** (lines 43-48): Particulate → fine detritus\n- **Fine detritus dissolution** (lines 50-66): Dissolved → DOC/DON\n- **Mineralization** (lines 68-113): Decomposer-driven DOC/DON → TAN\n  - Monod kinetics with DO and C substrate limitation\n  - Microfauna boost factor (line 81)\n\n- **Nitrification cascade** (lines 115-234):\n  - **AOB pathway**: TAN → nitrite (line 197), O2 cost = 3.43 mg O2/mg N (line 127)\n  - **NOB pathway**: nitrite → nitrate (line 232), O2 cost = 1.14 mg O2/mg N (line 129)\n  - **Comammox pathway**: TAN → nitrate directly (line 200), O2 cost = **4.57 mg O2/mg N** (line 128)\n  \n- **Guild biomass tracking** (lines 241-261):\n  - Ammonia oxidizers (AOB)\n  - Nitrite oxidizers (NOB)\n  - Comammox organisms\n\n- **Alkalinity consumption**: 0.1428 meq/mg N (hardcoded in chemistry.rs, line 123)\n\n---\n\n### 3. AMMONIA SPECIATION - IMPLEMENTED\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/chemistry.rs` (lines 23-27)\n\n```rust\nlet pka = 0.09018 + 2729.92 / (273.2 + temp_c);\nlet fraction_nh3 = 1.0 / (1.0 + 10.0_f64.powf(pka - ph));\ntan_mg_l * fraction_nh3\n```\n\n- **pKa formula**: Temperature-dependent (Henderson-Hasselbalch variant)\n- **Fraction calculation**: Uses 10^(pKa - pH) inverse\n- Function: `compute_nh3_mg_l(tan_mg_l, ph, temp_c)`\n\n---\n\n### 4. DISSOLVED OXYGEN - FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/dissolved_oxygen.rs`\n\n- **DO saturation table** (lines 5-6 in temperature.rs):\n  - 0°C → 14.6 mg/L\n  - 10°C → 11.3 mg/L\n  - 20°C → 9.1 mg/L\n  - 30°C → 7.6 mg/L\n  - Linear interpolation between points (lines 15-22)\n\n- **Reaeration** (lines 22-24 in DO system):\n  - k_la = base KLA + aeration boost\n  - Delta DO = k_la × (sat - current) × volume\n\n- **Photosynthesis** (lines 30-38):\n  - O2 production from photosynthetic biomass\n  - Only when light is on\n  - Multiplied by light intensity index\n\n- **Respiration** (lines 26-29):\n  - Background BOD from all respiring biomass\n  - Constants: mg O2 per g biomass per hour\n\n---\n\n### 5. pH AND ALKALINITY - FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/chemistry.rs` (lines 7-21)\n\n- **pH from alkalinity and DIC**:\n  ```rust\n  pH = 6.3 + log10(alkalinity_meq_l) - log10(dic_mmol_l)\n  ```\n  - Clamped to range 5.5-8.5\n\n- **Nitrification alkalinity consumption**: 0.1428 meq/mg N (line 256 in presets)\n  - Applied in nitrogen_cycle.rs lines 123-125, 148-150, 181-185\n\n- **Photosynthesis/respiration affect DIC** (lines 35-54):\n  - Respiration increases DIC\n  - Photosynthesis decreases DIC\n  - Alkalinity feedback: 0.0002 meq per mg C (line 5)\n\n---\n\n### 6. SUBSTRATE - FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/substrate.rs`\n\n- **Four substrate types** (lines 4-8):\n  - InertSand\n  - InertGravel\n  - ActivePlanted\n  - CoarsePorous\n\n- **Multi-layer support** (lines 12-22):\n  - 1-3 configurable layers per tank\n  - Each layer has:\n    - depth_cm\n    - nutrient_store_mg_n_total\n    - nutrient_store_mg_p_total\n    - cation_exchange_capacity_index\n    - detritus_trapping_index\n    - colonizable_area_cm2\n    - low_oxygen_tendency_index\n    - grazing_surface_index\n\n- **Plant nutrient uptake** (plant_growth.rs lines 251-265):\n  - Substrate N and P pools tracked\n  - Root-feeding plants preferentially access substrate nutrients\n\n---\n\n### 7. PLANTS - FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/plant_growth.rs`\n\n- **Two guilds** (biology.rs line 15-17):\n  - FastStem: 90% water-column, 10% substrate uptake (lines 214-216)\n  - RootFeedingRosette: 10% water-column, 90% substrate uptake (lines 219-223)\n\n- **Growth rate limiting factors** (lines 61-67):\n  - Light factor (lines 98-108): Half-saturation on light intensity\n  - Temperature factor (lines 272-278): Gaussian response, optimum 25°C\n  - Nutrient limitation (lines 44-52):\n    - N limitation (half-sat = 8 mg)\n    - P limitation (half-sat = 1.2 mg)\n    - C limitation (half-sat = 20 mg)\n  - Habitat index (lines 110-143):\n    - FastStem: 0.95 (tolerant)\n    - RootFeedingRosette: depends on substrate depth, CEC, active layer bonus\n\n- **Plant stress tracking** (lines 87-94):\n  - Health index that responds to limiting conditions\n  - Recovery rate 0.03/day in good conditions\n  - Decline rate 0.08/day in stress\n\n---\n\n### 8. ALGAE & PERIPHYTON - FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/algae_growth.rs`\n\n- **Two algae pools** (biology.rs lines 30-34):\n  - Suspended biomass (water column)\n  - Periphyton 