- log10(dic_mmol_l)\n  ```\n  - Clamped to range 5.5-8.5\n\n- **Nitrification alkalinity consumption**: 0.1428 meq/mg N (line 256 in presets)\n  - Applied in nitrogen_cycle.rs lines 123-125, 148-150, 181-185\n\n- **Photosynthesis/respiration affect DIC** (lines 35-54):\n  - Respiration increases DIC\n  - Photosynthesis decreases DIC\n  - Alkalinity feedback: 0.0002 meq per mg C (line 5)\n\n---\n\n### 6. SUBSTRATE - FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/substrate.rs`\n\n- **Four substrate types** (lines 4-8):\n  - InertSand\n  - InertGravel\n  - ActivePlanted\n  - CoarsePorous\n\n- **Multi-layer support** (lines 12-22):\n  - 1-3 configurable layers per tank\n  - Each layer has:\n    - depth_cm\n    - nutrient_store_mg_n_total\n    - nutrient_store_mg_p_total\n    - cation_exchange_capacity_index\n    - detritus_trapping_index\n    - colonizable_area_cm2\n    - low_oxygen_tendency_index\n    - grazing_surface_index\n\n- **Plant nutrient uptake** (plant_growth.rs lines 251-265):\n  - Substrate N and P pools tracked\n  - Root-feeding plants preferentially access substrate nutrients\n\n---\n\n### 7. PLANTS - FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/plant_growth.rs`\n\n- **Two guilds** (biology.rs line 15-17):\n  - FastStem: 90% water-column, 10% substrate uptake (lines 214-216)\n  - RootFeedingRosette: 10% water-column, 90% substrate uptake (lines 219-223)\n\n- **Growth rate limiting factors** (lines 61-67):\n  - Light factor (lines 98-108): Half-saturation on light intensity\n  - Temperature factor (lines 272-278): Gaussian response, optimum 25°C\n  - Nutrient limitation (lines 44-52):\n    - N limitation (half-sat = 8 mg)\n    - P limitation (half-sat = 1.2 mg)\n    - C limitation (half-sat = 20 mg)\n  - Habitat index (lines 110-143):\n    - FastStem: 0.95 (tolerant)\n    - RootFeedingRosette: depends on substrate depth, CEC, active layer bonus\n\n- **Plant stress tracking** (lines 87-94):\n  - Health index that responds to limiting conditions\n  - Recovery rate 0.03/day in good conditions\n  - Decline rate 0.08/day in stress\n\n---\n\n### 8. ALGAE & PERIPHYTON - FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/algae_growth.rs`\n\n- **Two algae pools** (biology.rs lines 30-34):\n  - Suspended biomass (water column)\n  - Periphyton biomass (surfaces)\n\n- **Growth rate limiting** (lines 16-49):\n  - Light factor (lines 113-123)\n  - Temperature factor (lines 17-21): Optimum 27°C\n  - Plant shading (lines 22-30): Up to 70% reduction\n  - Nutrient limitation (lines 31-38): N and P half-saturation\n  - Microfauna grazing (lines 39-41): Up to 30% reduction\n\n- **Periphyton capacity model** (lines 64-73):\n  - Grows on colonizable surfaces\n  - Capacity = area × 6 g/m²\n  - Capacity-dependent growth limiting (line 72)\n\n- **Nuisance index** (lines 97-108):\n  - 55% suspended pressure + 45% periphyton pressure\n  - Used for event emission\n\n---\n\n### 9. MICROBES & MICROFAUNA - FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs` + `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/microfauna.rs`\n\n**Microbes** (tracked in biology.rs lines 36-43):\n- decomposer_biomass_g: Heterotrophic bacteria\n- ammonia_oxidizer_biomass_g: AOB guild\n- nitrite_oxidizer_biomass_g: NOB guild\n- comammox_biomass_g: Comammox guild\n\n**Nitrifier dynamics** (nitrogen_cycle.rs):\n- Growth yields: 0.001 g/mg N (lines 243, 250)\n- Decay rates: 0.003/hour (lines 245, 252)\n- Monod kinetics (lines 315-324)\n- Temperature and pH factors (lines 278-293)\n- Biofilter maturity tracking (lines 328-344)\n\n**Microfauna** (microfauna.rs lines 10-56):\n- Population index: 0-1 scale\n- Grazing pressure index: Function of population and food\n- Effects:\n  - Boost mineralization efficiency (nitrogen_cycle.rs line 81)\n  - Consume periphyton (lines 45-49)\n  - Consume some detritus (lines 51-55)\n  - Grazed down by shrimp (lines 28-32)\n\n---\n\n### 10. SHRIMP - FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs`\n\n**Population structure** (biology.rs lines 52-74):\n- adults_count\n- juveniles_count\n- berried_females_count\n- egg_cohorts (clutch tracking for invariant enforcement)\n\n**Physiological state** (lines 56-73):\n- condition_index (0-1): Overall health/fitness\n- molt_stress_index (0-1): Ecdysis risk\n- reproductive_readiness_index (0-1): Spawning probability\n\n**Temperature-dependent reproduction** (shrimp.rs lines 505-528):\n- Optimal range: 22-26°C (defaults)\n- Penalty starts at 28°C\n- Penalty full at 33°C\n- Gaussian response within optimal range\n\n**Lifecycle stages** (lines 58-82):\n1. **Feeding**: Periphyton & detritus grazing (lines 119-140)\n2. **Condition update**: Multi-factor (food, DO, ammonia, temperature, GH, stability) (lines 142-192)\n3. **Molt stress**: GH, instability, condition, thermal stress (lines 194-231)\n4. **Reproductive readiness**: Temperature × condition × stability × molt (lines 233-248)\n5. **Spawning**: Stochastic, multi-factor gates (lines 250-301)\n6. **Egg development**: Duration-dependent (21 days default) with hatch success factors (lines 303-404)\n7. **Juvenile recruitment**: Maturation at ~90 days (lines 406-421)\n8. **Mortality**: Base rate + stress-scaled (lines 423-458)\n\n**Stress tracking** (lines 10-50):\n- Hourly accumulation of NH3, nitrite, low-DO, heat, instability\n- Resets daily\n\n**Stability tracker** (lines 84-115):\n- Monitors swings in: temperature, pH, GH, DO\n- Instability index used for stress calculation\n\n---\n\n### SUMMARY TABLE\n\n| System | File | Status | Key Constants | Formula/Kinetics |\n|--------|------|--------|----------------|------------------|\n| 1. Temperature | temperature.rs | ✓ COMPLETE | 4186 J/L·K, 3600s | UA-based heat transfer + deadband heater |\n| 2. Nitrogen Cycle | nitrogen_cycle.rs | ✓ COMPLETE | 4.57 mg O2/mg N | Feed→mineralization→TAN→NO2→NO3, Monod kinetics |\n| 3. Ammonia Speciation | chemistry.rs | ✓ COMPLETE | pKa=0.09018+2729.92/(273.2+T) | NH3 fraction = 1/(1+10^(pKa-pH)) |\n| 4. Dissolved Oxygen | dissolved_oxygen.rs | ✓ COMPLETE | DO_sat: 0→14.6, 10→11.3, 20→9.1, 30→7.6 | Reaeration + photosynthesis - respiration |\n| 5. pH & Alkalinity | chemistry.rs | ✓ COMPLETE | 0.1428 meq/mg N, 0.0002 meq/mg C | pH from Alk & DIC, alk consumed by nitrification |\n| 6. Substrate | substrate.rs | ✓ COMPLETE | 4 types, 1-3 layers, N/P pools | CEC, detritus trapping, colonizable area |\n| 7. Plants | plant_growth.rs | ✓ COMPLETE | FastStem (0.08/day), Rosette (0.06/day) | 2 guilds, light/temp/nutrient/habitat limited |\n| 8. Algae/Periphyton | algae_growth.rs | ✓ COMPLETE | Capacity 6 g/m², suspended 0.2/day | Light/temp/nutrient/shading limited, microfauna grazed |\n| 9. Microbes | nitrogen_cycle.rs | ✓ COMPLETE | AOB/NOB/Comammox with yields & decay | Monod kinetics, maturity factor, guild growth/decay |\n| 10. Shrimp | shrimp.rs | ✓ COMPLETE | Optimal 22-26°C, penalty 28→33°C, 21-day eggs | Condition/molt/repro driven by multifactor gates |\n\n---\n\n### CONCLUSION\n\n**ALL 10 SYSTEMS FULLY IMPLEMENTED** with correct formulas, constants, and stoichiometry. The simulation is comprehensive and internally consistent. No missing components detected."}],"totalDurationMs":55540,"totalTokens":62271,"totalToolUseCount":22,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1029,"cache_read_input_tokens":57431,"output_tokens":3811,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1029},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
